{"text": " How do tariffs work? Tariffs can be dollar amount, or a percentage of the cost of items. Most monkey countries use percentage tariffs, but they call them ad valorem. To make monkeys sound smart, tariffs can get really specific. Unripe banana can have different tariffs to ripe ones, even though they both banana. Even banana cannot escape bureaucracy. Trade terms. When monkey government not use tariffs, this is called free trade. When monkey country export more banana than they import, this called a trade surplus. But when monkey country import more banana than export, this is called trade deficit. What happens when tariffs are used? Price of imported banana goes up. Monkeyland banana stores happy, as there are no more cheap bananas to compete with. But less banana competition can also mean banana quality go down. Local banana becomes monkey's only option. Local price can also go up to just under banana land banana. Monkeyland monkey's frustrated. Monkeys have to choose between paying more for good banana or eat worse banana for cheap.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.72, "text": " How do tariffs work?", "tokens": [50363, 1374, 466, 29240, 670, 30, 50449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13275461376837963, "compression_ratio": 1.7103174603174602, "no_speech_prob": 0.003849627682939172}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 1.72, "end": 5.0200000000000005, "text": " Tariffs can be dollar amount, or a percentage of the cost of items.", "tokens": [50449, 14110, 10203, 460, 307, 8872, 2033, 11, 393, 257, 5873, 286, 262, 1575, 286, 3709, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13275461376837963, "compression_ratio": 1.7103174603174602, "no_speech_prob": 0.003849627682939172}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 5.0200000000000005, "end": 9.8, "text": " Most monkey countries use percentage tariffs, but they call them ad valorem.", "tokens": [50614, 4042, 21657, 2678, 779, 5873, 29240, 11, 475, 484, 869, 606, 512, 1188, 29625, 13, 5085